# Angular — reservation-frontend

Apply these rules when developing `reservation-frontend` and any future frontend code in this repository.

## Project layout

```
parcial_2/
├── docker-compose-desarrollo.yml       # frontend service on port 4200
└── reservation-frontend/
    ├── angular.json                    # Angular 21, prefix app
    ├── package.json                    # Angular 21.2, RxJS 7.8, Vitest
    ├── tsconfig.json                   # strict: true, strictTemplates
    ├── Dockerfile                      # Node 24, ng serve :4200
    └── src/
        ├── main.ts
        ├── index.html
        ├── styles.css
        └── app/
            ├── app.ts                  # Root standalone component
            ├── app.config.ts           # provideRouter, provideHttpClient
            ├── app.routes.ts
            ├── core/                   # App-wide singletons (create as needed)
            ├── shared/                 # Reusable UI, pipes, directives (create as needed)
            ├── domain/                 # Entities, ports, use-case contracts
            ├── data/                   # HTTP clients, mappers, repository impl
            ├── features/               # Feature slices (pages + presentation)
            ├── model/                  # API DTOs (align with backend records)
            └── service/                # Legacy; migrate to data/ or features/
```
## Language and naming
- **All** class, interface, enum, record, method, field, and parameter names **must be in English** 

**Stack:** Angular 21 (standalone APIs), TypeScript 5.9 (`strict: true`), RxJS 7.8, Vitest, Prettier.

**Backend API (reservation-backend):** base path `/api/reservations` — mirror DTO names and shapes from backend (`CreateReservationRequest`, `ReservationResponse`).

**Runtime:** local dev `http://localhost:8080`; in Docker Compose use the backend service hostname instead of `localhost` (configure via environment, not hardcoded in components).

