## Clean Architecture (layers)

Dependencies point **inward**: Presentation → Application → Domain ← Data/Infrastructure.

| Layer | Folder | Responsibility |
|-------|--------|----------------|
| **Domain** | `domain/` | Business entities, enums, repository **ports** (interfaces), use-case contracts. No Angular or HTTP imports. |
| **Application** | `features/*/application/` or feature services | Orchestrates use cases; depends on domain ports only. |
| **Data** | `data/` | HTTP API clients, DTO mappers, repository **implementations** that satisfy domain ports. |
| **Presentation** | `features/*/pages/`, `features/*/components/` | Components, templates, route config. Delegates to application layer; no direct `HttpClient` in templates. |
| **Core** | `core/` | Interceptors, guards, global error handler, environment tokens. |
| **Shared** | `shared/` | Dumb/reusable UI components, pipes, directives with no feature-specific business logic. |

**Rules:**

- Components **must not** call `HttpClient` directly; inject a repository, facade, or use-case service.
- Map API DTOs (`model/`) to domain entities in the **data** layer when they diverge; keep presentation unaware of JSON shape details.
- Feature folders are **vertical slices** (e.g. `features/reservations/`); avoid a flat `components/` dump of unrelated screens.

