## SOLID in Angular

| Principle | Application |
|-----------|-------------|
| **S — Single Responsibility** | One reason to change per class: a component renders UI; a service orchestrates one use case; a repository handles one aggregate's persistence. |
| **O — Open/Closed** | Extend behavior via new implementations of ports (e.g. `ReservationRepository`) or strategy classes; avoid modifying stable components for every variant. |
| **L — Liskov Substitution** | Implementations of interfaces/abstract classes must honor the contract (same inputs/outputs, no surprising side effects). |
| **I — Interface Segregation** | Small, focused ports (`ReservationReader`, `ReservationWriter`) instead of one god interface with unused methods. |
| **D — Dependency Inversion** | Depend on abstractions (`InjectionToken<ReservationRepository>` or abstract class); wire concrete HTTP implementations in `app.config.ts` or feature providers. |

Prefer **`inject()`** and constructor injection; register implementations with `providers` / `provide*` functions, not `new` in components.

